  "rationale": "w187/effects-union (PR #169) unions campaign/signed-magnitudes and campaign/combined ON TOP OF #161 and #164, so node effects now drive the three academic rates (research-rate, teach-rate, scribe-rate) and the two vitality primitives (lifespan, fertility), while the anti-requisites exclusion pair from #161 stays exactly as recorded there. Recorded from the tree MERGED WITH origin/main 1e2651a, not from the branch alone, per the w77 precedent. provenance.contentHash e8442af2c5f91ae6f80ad9a178e0e451 -> a new value: node.json gained one authored COST -- a teach-rate of -192 on pn-the-nameless -- and the revision is a digest over the values, so the previous baselines refuse before reading a metric. THIS FILE IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A BALANCE CLAIM: release-plan.md forbids a balance claim before 0.5.0, and nothing here is one. Neither parent branch could have recorded these numbers: combined's four negative-magnitude guard fixes were inert under a schema saying minimum 1, and signed-magnitudes' negative magnitudes were swallowed by routeYieldByForm's clamp. NO GOLDEN FIXTURE WAS REGENERATED. balance-gate-ascension-v1 is deliberately NOT re-recorded, the same carve-out #161 and #72 record: it carries a superseded rngRegistryHash, already fails on main for that older unrelated reason, and balance/README.md marks its job not required to merge. The universe remains degenerate in the ways integration round 2 recorded and this change closes none of them.",
